  "description": "The \u0027dss_codeenvs_cached\u0027 dataset provides comprehensive information about cached code environments used within a data science platform. Each entry in the dataset represents a specific code environment, detailing its name, programming language, deployment mode, and owner. This dataset is particularly useful for managing and auditing code environments, ensuring that they are properly configured and maintained. It includes information on the Python interpreter version and core packages set, which are crucial for compatibility and performance. The dataset also tracks the file path and size of each environment, aiding in storage management. Additionally, it records the projects where each code environment is used, the total instances of the environment, and provides a direct URL for access. This dataset is valuable for administrators and developers who need to monitor and optimize the use of code environments across various projects, ensuring efficient resource allocation and compliance with organizational standards.",
